      "name": null,
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}5\\cdot {2}^{n-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $1$ to $3.$ So, computing the terms for $n=1,2,3$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}5\\cdot {2}^{n-1} & =(5\\cdot {2}^{1-1})+(5\\cdot {2}^{2-1})+(5\\cdot {2}^{3-1}) \\\\  & =(5\\cdot {2}^{0})+(5\\cdot {2}^{1})+(5\\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 1)+(5\\cdot 2)+(5\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =5+10+20 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
