      "dom_id": "question-66995",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Express $S=8+16+24+⋯+80+88$ in sigma notation.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence\n\n$$\n8,\\,16,\\,24,\\,…,\\,80,\\,88.\n$$\n\n are multiples of $8,$ and since $88÷8=11,$ there are $11$ terms in total. \n\nTherefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=8n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=11.$ Indeed: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =8(1)=8 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =8(2)=16 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =8(3)=24 \\\\  & \\,\\,⋮ \\\\ {a}_{10} & =8(10)=80 \\\\ {a}_{11} & =8(11)=88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S=8+16+24+⋯+80+88={\\sum }_{n=1}^{11}8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
